"""Manuel Academy High School Science 9-12 - course design specification.

This module is the hand-authored source of truth for the four-course sequence.
`build_authoring_set.py` expands it into a schema-set 2.0.0 authoring set.

Every unit declares:
  title, essential_question, phenomenon, topics (exactly 6), performance_task,
  standards (primary), spiral (secondary), investigation.

`spiral` lists performance expectations the unit touches without owning. The build
classifies each entry against the global teaching order: an entry first taught in
or before this unit is REINFORCEMENT, and one first taught later is a PREVIEW. The
two are never labelled the same way, and only primary standards are assessed.

`investigation` declares the Day 7 laboratory or field work:
  title        - what the learner does
  materials    - household-safe materials only
  hazards      - list of (kind, description, mitigation); kind is one of
                 physical | chemical | online | financial | privacy | emotional
  supervision  - none | nearby-adult | direct-adult
  visibility   - summary | confirmation-required | direct-observation
  stop         - extra stop conditions beyond the global set
  sequence     - REQUIRED ordered steps the learner reads before handling anything.
                 Where two hazards must not meet, the ordering, the time gap, the
                 change of surface, and the disposal of the POURED SAMPLES are stated
                 here as procedure, not left to a mitigation note.
  disposal     - REQUIRED clean-up and disposal, including cool-down where a material
                 stays reactive after the run. Nothing warm or oxidising is ever sealed.
  alternative  - REQUIRED no-special-equipment path to the same learning target
  data_source  - where real numbers come from; never fabricated results

Every hazard, mitigation, supervision level, stop condition, sequence step, disposal
step, and alternative reaches the LEARNER through the student-visible safety brief the
build emits on the investigation day. `safety_privacy` remains the guardian record; it
is stripped from the student projection by the 2.0.0 contract, so it is never the only
place actionable safety lives.
"""

